      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T06:06:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That can\u0027t be right in the context of VPN. In your case the caller is Vpn.java which lives in the system server, but it will need to redact for the app, which may be running in another user.\n\n\nI think the only solution is to pass the UID instead of the package name. VPN can know that because it has the user handle for this VPN and the name of the app. Then you make the API in ConnectivityManager take UID PID, and VPN passes -1 for the PID, and I think it will work.\nThis will also simplify your code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2067,
        "startChar": 47,
        "endLine": 2067,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "267673cb1976efc61cdbe9ba16a2660036aedbe5",
